{
  "id": "chinese-room-argument",
  "term": "Chinese Room argument",
  "definition": "The Chinese Room argument is a philosophical challenge to the idea that computation alone produces genuine understanding. It uses a scenario in which symbols are manipulated by rules without access to their meaning, to argue that isolated symbol processing may imitate language use without true semantic understanding.",
